# Byte-exact checkout for every file: no line-ending conversion.
# Several files are verified by SHA-256 (configs pinned by tests/test_pretrain_check.py, pageocr/protected_manifest.json,
# data/manifests/datasets.json, the experiment records); converting LF <-> CRLF on checkout would break those checks.
* -text

# Binary assets (no diff, no merge)
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.tif binary
*.tiff binary

# Trained checkpoints are NOT in this repository (.gitignore). If the owner decides to publish one with Git LFS
# (DEPLOYMENT.md, step 1), `git lfs track "runs/experiment_002a/best.pth"` adds the matching rule here, and
# `git add -f runs/experiment_002a/best.pth` stages it while every other weight file stays ignored.
